Provenance of the crate hclconf

Source: a copy of the crate hclconf of Hune (https://github.com/ProcurAuth/hune), version 0.1.1, with its tests.
Hune and Pupitre are projects of the same organisation and have the same licence (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

Changes in this copy:

1. The paragraph numbers in the comments are the paragraphs of section 6 of the Pupitre specification
   (docs/06-configuration.md). Section 6 keeps the numbers of the engine paragraphs of Hune: 6.3 is the HCL subset,
   6.5 the forms, 6.14 the errors, 6.18 the read modes, 6.23 the environment, 6.25 the limits.
2. A labelled block can hold one level of labelled blocks, for example `command "restart" { param "grace" { } }`
   (6.12). In Hune, a labelled block must be at the top of the file. A deeper level is still refused.
   `ResolvedKey` and `BlockInstance` have the new member `sub_label`. `Checked` has the new functions `get_in_sub`,
   `block_in_sub` and `sub_labels`. The reference writes `command "<id>".param "<name>".type`.
   The test file tests/nested_labels.rs covers the change.
3. A test value names no other product.

The crate has its own parser of the HCL subset of 6.3. It has no dependency.

Edition: 2021. The crate stays on the edition 2021 because src/env.rs calls std::env::remove_var.
This function is unsafe from the edition 2024, and each crate of the workspace forbids unsafe code.

The three behaviours of 6.1 are built in:

1. A duration has exactly one integer and one unit (ms, s, m or h). The text "1m 30s", the unit
   us and the unit ns are not valid.
2. A block can depend on a mode key, as an attribute can.
3. A boolean key can be a mode key.

Only src/env.rs reads the environment (6.23). The tests of the crate are in src/ and in tests/.
